        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Personal</td><td>Name</td><td>Essameldin Salama</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Personal</td><td>Title</td><td>Senior Strategic Advisor | MBA, BSc | Program Manager</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Contact</td><td>Phone</td><td>+974 66205660</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Contact</td><td>Email</td><td>essamslama@hotmail.com</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Contact</td><td>Location</td><td>Doha, Qatar</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Contact</td><td>LinkedIn</td><td>https://www.linkedin.com/in/essameldin56/</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Stats</td><td>Years Multi-Market Experience</td><td>34+</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Stats</td><td>Mega Capital Programs Managed</td><td>$10B+</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Stats</td><td>Member Since Institute of Internal Auditors</td><td>1996</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Profile</td><td>About Me</td><td>I help organizations, leaders, and ambitious professionals solve complexity, improve performance, and achieve meaningful transformation through practical executive experience, strategic thinking, and disciplined execution.<br><br>With over 34 years of multi-market experience across the Gulf and Egypt, my background includes supporting major organizations in government, infrastructure, ports, and petroleum operations—where decisions carry real operational and financial impact.<br><br>I am best engaged when the challenge is serious, complexity is high, and results matter. I am also passionate about helping middle managers break career stagnation and rise toward senior executive roles.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience</td><td>Education</td><td>MBA</td><td>Woolf University (In Progress)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience</td><td>Education</td><td>BSc Commerce, Accounting & Economics</td><td>Alexandria University</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience</td><td>Education</td><td>Professional Member</td><td>Institute of Internal Auditors (since 1996)</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience</td><td>Expertise</td><td>Finance Transformation & Modernization</td><td>The transition from legacy cash-based accounting to modern, accrual-based financial frameworks is fraught with operational risk. I specialize in orchestrating these massive paradigm shifts for government and mega-corporate entities. By leading IPSAS (International Public Sector Accounting Standards) first-time adoptions, I ensure that financial transparency meets international scrutiny.<br><br>- IPSAS Adoption: End-to-end management of accrual accounting transitions in public sectors.<br>- ERP Alignment: Translating C-suite business requirements into actionable Oracle/SAP technical architectures.<br>- Process Redesign: Eliminating systemic bottlenecks in capital expenditure cycles.<br>- Change Management: Cultivating a culture of financial accountability across non-financial engineering teams.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience</td><td>Expertise</td><td>Strategic Planning & Project Financial Controls</td><td>Managing multi-billion-dollar infrastructure portfolios requires far more than basic budgeting; it demands predictive financial modeling and rigorous commercial controls. I have engineered integrated five-year forecasts and capital deployment frameworks for projects that reshaped the skylines and coastlines of the UAE and Qatar.<br><br>- Zero-Based Budgeting: Establishing absolute cost justification for massive capital outlays.<br>- Cash Flow Forecasting: Advanced predictive modeling to prevent liquidity crunches in offshore mega-projects.<br>- Commercial Costing: Bridging the gap between engineering estimates and actual financial drawdowns.<br>- Variance Analysis: Implementing strict tolerance thresholds for contractor milestones.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Experience</td><td>Expertise</td><td>Governance, Risk & Decision Support</td><td>True executive leadership relies on unimpeachable data and robust risk management. Drawing upon my foundational years in forensic auditing at Arthur Andersen, I design internal control environments that protect organizational integrity while enabling, rather than hindering, rapid scale.<br><br>- Board-Level Reporting: Distilling complex operational data into actionable C-suite financial narratives.<br>- Internal Controls: Architecting fraud-resistant, compliant workflows across decentralized operations.<br>- Policy Development: Writing the operational rulebooks that govern organizational finance.<br>- Executive Mentorship: Coaching operational directors to understand the financial implications of their decisions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Projects</td><td>Experience</td><td>Finance Transformation Program (Public Works Authority 'Ashghal')</td><td>Serving as Program Manager and Senior Strategic Advisor, acting as a catalyst for governance enhancement and performance improvement across a major public-sector organization.<br><br><strong>CHALLENGE:</strong> The organization needed to transition to accrual-based accounting (IPSAS) and modernize financial governance.<br><br><strong>ACTION:</strong> Led the strategic alignment between executive business needs and technical ERP capabilities.<br><br><strong>RESULT:</strong> Successfully established a culture of accountability and improved executive visibility into capital deployment.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Projects</td><td>Experience</td><td>KPIZ - Khalifa Port & Industrial Zone (Abu Dhabi Ports Company)</td><td>Held VP Finance role leading Project Financial Controls, overseeing financial governance of capital programs exceeding multi-billion-dollar values.<br><br><strong>CHALLENGE:</strong> Managing the financial controls and cash flow forecasting for an unprecedented offshore port mega-project.<br><br><strong>ACTION:</strong> Developed and implemented rigorous project financial controls from scratch.<br><br><strong>RESULT:</strong> Delivered high-fidelity financial visibility to the Board of Directors.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Projects</td><td>Experience</td><td>Flagship Development Portfolios (Nakheel – UAE)</td><td>As Financial Planning & Reporting Manager, delivered comprehensive five-year forecasts for world-class mega projects during a historic expansion phase.<br><br><strong>CHALLENGE:</strong> The rapid scale of development required highly complex, long-term financial modeling.<br><br><strong>ACTION:</strong> Engineered integrated five-year forecasts covering both financial and commercial dimensions.<br><br><strong>RESULT:</strong> Provided the critical data backbone needed for Board-level reporting and investment decisions.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Projects</td><td>Experience</td><td>Finance & Commercial Management (Major Petroleum & Gas Sector)</td><td>Directed financial strategies, budgeting, and performance management for large-scale petroleum operations, ensuring strict compliance and cost control.<br><br><strong>CHALLENGE:</strong> Navigating volatile market conditions while maintaining strict budgetary control over capital-intensive exploration and production projects.<br><br><strong>ACTION:</strong> Implemented comprehensive performance measurement systems and variance analysis frameworks for operational budgeting.<br><br><strong>RESULT:</strong> Optimized cash flow forecasting, eliminated structural inefficiencies, and safeguarded critical investments.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Projects</td><td>Experience</td><td>Senior Accountant (Arthur Andersen – Egypt)</td><td>Established early career foundation in rigorous financial auditing, internal controls, and enterprise accounting standards at a top global firm.<br><br><strong>CHALLENGE:</strong> Ensuring precise compliance and financial integrity for rapidly scaling corporate clients.<br><br><strong>ACTION:</strong> Executed detailed audits, identified systemic weaknesses in client financial reporting, and recommended robust internal controls.<br><br><strong>RESULT:</strong> Built a strong foundation in forensic accounting, risk mitigation, and executive-level financial reporting.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Testimonials</td><td>Former Executive Colleague, Abu Dhabi Ports Company</td><td>Essameldin brings an unparalleled depth of strategic vision and operational discipline. His work in establishing our project financial controls completely transformed our executive visibility during a high-growth phase.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>Testimonials</td><td>Finance Leadership, Public Works Authority 'Ashghal'</td><td>A master at bridging complex business needs with system solutions. He didn't just redesign our finance operations; he cultivated a culture of true accountability and performance.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>FAQ</td><td>What types of organizations do you typically advise?</td><td>I primarily advise major public sector entities, global infrastructure developers, and large-scale petroleum and gas corporations across the Gulf and Egypt. My experience is heavily concentrated in environments managing multi-billion dollar capital programs.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>FAQ</td><td>Do you handle ERP implementation directly?</td><td>While I don't configure the code for systems like Oracle or SAP directly, my expertise lies in the critical step before and during implementation: translating complex C-suite financial needs into precise technical requirements to ensure the final system actually serves the executive vision.</td></tr>
        <tr><td>Home</td><td>FAQ</td><td>How do you approach finance transformation?</td><td>My approach centers on deeply embedding financial accountability throughout the entire organization, not just the finance department. From leading first-time IPSAS adoptions to redesigning operational workflows, the goal is total structural alignment between strategy and execution.</td></tr>
